  "_rounds_at_arming_means": "The (subject, round) pairs that EXISTED when the scheme was armed, PINNED rather than recomputed from git at read time — the same reason `rounds_to_termination` is pinned. ⛔ WHY IT HAD TO BE PINNED (backlog #341, 2026-10-22): `tree_at()` asked git what the tree held at `armed_at`, and a SQUASH MERGE destroys that answer — every file a squash carries enters the target branch's history at the squash commit's date, so review documents that existed before arming look newer than it. MEASURED: docs/reviews/claude/memory-index-budget-r1-claude.md was added by 49b7b267 (2026-10-19) on the pre-merge branch and by ee0e461b (2026-10-21) on master, and trigger 1 then named memory-index-budget as newly starved when its rounds 1, 2 and 3 all predate arming. No better DATE fixes this: the information is destroyed, not mis-stamped. DERIVED 2026-10-22 from commit 5d957db8 (2026-10-20 08:27:49 -0700) on branch decision-route-escalation, whose history the squash did not rewrite, through the SAME `rounds_in_paths` grammar the live corpus is read with. ⚠ It is a SNAPSHOT of one instant and is not re-derived: re-arming the scheme means recording a new `armed_at` AND a new inventory together, or the two describe different moments."
